    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11128": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Housing and Residence Life for Operations",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Assistant Director of Housing and Residence Life for Operations Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Assistant Director of Housing and Residence Life for Operations Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Assistant Director of Housing and Residence Life for Operations Campus: Florham Campus, Madison, NJ Department: Residence Life-Florham Hiring Manager: Rebecca Valenzuela Hiring Manager Title: Universidy Director of Housing and Residence Life College: Position Type: Professional Administrative Grade: 26 FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $52,015.00 General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, paid time off, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: Under the direction of the University Director of Housing and Residence Life, the Assistant Director of Housing and Residence Life for Operations is a key member of the Housing and Residence Life leadership team responsible for the overall administration and coordination of housing operations for the Florham Campus. This position oversees all aspects of the housing assignment process, occupancy management, meal plan administration, housing applications, data management, reporting, and operational processes that support the residential experience. The Assistant Director serves as the primary functional lead for housing management systems and operational procedures while collaborating with campus partners to ensure efficient, student-centered service delivery. This position develops and implements housing policies and procedures, analyzes occupancy trends and data, and supports strategic planning related to enrollment and residential capacity. This is a 12-month, full-time professional position. Required Qualifications: 1. Master’s degree required in Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs, Business Administration, Public Administration, or related field. 2. Two to four years of progressively responsible experience in Housing and Residence Life, Student Affairs, or a related administrative area. 3. Demonstrated experience with housing management software StarRez and student information systems. 4. Strong analytical skills with experience interpreting data, preparing reports, and utilizing data to support strategic decision-making. 5. Excellent organizational, project management, and problem-solving skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. 6. Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to effectively collaborate with students, faculty, staff, and campus partners. 7. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and handle sensitive student information. 8. Demonstrated commitment to customer service and continuous process improvement. 9. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends as required and participate in the professional staff on-call rotation. 10. Live-on accommodations are available but are not required for this position. 11. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 35 Posting Date: 08/26/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
