    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11025": {
      "title": "Adjuncts - Adjuncts for CFP Certificate program- Fall 2026",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Adjuncts - Adjuncts for CFP Certificate program- Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Adjuncts - Adjuncts for CFP Certificate program- Fall 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants need to also e-mail their resume and cover letter to the Dep’t Chair, Professor R. West at west@fdu.edu Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Adjuncts - Adjuncts for CFP Certificate program- Fall 2026 Campus: Florham Campus, Madison, NJ Department: Accounting, Tax & Law Department-Florham Hiring Manager: Ron West Hiring Manager Title: CFP Program Director College: Silberman College of Business Position Type: Faculty Grade: Adjunct FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Adjunct Faculty Salary: $ 2,166.67 per credit General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: Eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan, and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.), and State benefits such as NJ Sick Leave and State Short Term Disability benefits. Status: No Response Months Worked: No Response Job Summary: Adjunct instructors to teach on Zoom (and possibly in person on the Florham campus, NJ) for a graduate level CFP Certificate program that is a CFP Board registered program. Program consists of seven financial planning courses: General Principals, Income Tax, Estate & Gift, Retirement, Insurance, Investment, and the Capstone class. Required Qualifications: Person should be a CFP with extensive professional experience. Alternatively, hold a JD with a focus on the subject class teaching. Other financial designations a plus. Teaching experience preferred. Exceptions evaluated in special cases. If interested, send resume to Prof Ron West at west@fdu.edu Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 06/25/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants need to also e-mail their resume and cover letter to the Dep’t Chair, Professor R. West at west@fdu.edu Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Other Document Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
