      "title": "Adjunct Professor - OTD---Spring 2026",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Adjunct Professor - OTD---Spring 2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Adjunct Professor - OTD---Spring 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Adjunct Professor - OTD---Spring 2026 Campus: Florham Campus, Madison, NJ Department: Occupational Therapy-Florham Hiring Manager: Dina Prisco Hiring Manager Title: Assistant Dean for Academic Affairs (Health Sciences) College: College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences Position Type: Faculty Grade: Adjunct FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Adjunct Faculty Salary: $1,500 per credit General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: Eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan, and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.), and State benefits such as NJ Sick Leave and State Short Term Disability benefits. Status: Part-Time Months Worked: No Response Job Summary: Fairleigh Dickinson University’s School of Pharmacy and Health Sciences is currently seeking adjunct professors to teach graduate-level courses within the Occupational Therapy Doctorate program. The selected candidate will teach courses covering occupational therapy concepts, advocacy, healthcare management, pediatric rehabilitation and/or adult rehabilitation. The selected candidate will be responsible for assessing student performance and providing feedback on course assignments. The classes will be held during the Spring, Summer, and Fall semesters. Classes meet in-person on weekdays and span across either 12- or 15- week semesters. The overall commitment entails three hours of teaching per week, along with availability for office hours. Required Qualifications: ·A doctoral degree in occupational therapy or related major awarded by an institution accredited by a USDE -recognized regional accrediting body. At least two years clinical experience in the field of OT. Clinical experience in physical rehabilitation, hand therapy, neurorehabilitation, geriatrics, and/or homecare is preferred. · Initially certified by NBCOT and be eligible for OT Licensure in New Jersey. · Demonstrated experience and ability to adapt teaching to various learning styles and levels of learners is highly desirable. · Prior teaching experience is strongly preferred. · Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. If interested, please contact Dr. Ilana Beitscher at i.beitscher@fdu.edu Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 10/14/2025 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Other Document Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
